<speak>Thank you. I'll keep to the main points. From our review, your aim is to cut equity exposure and smooth out portfolio swings, while keeping flexibility for personal needs. That's what we're working towards here. With Summit Global Equity <sub alias="ee tee eff">ETF</sub>, the underlying global shares can fall together in a broad market downturn, so diversification won't prevent the holding from dropping in value. Do you understand that the underlying shares can fall together, even though the fund is diversified?</speak>